From c742b62bb2cc31ad2efd62e93889fa913f505d1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:48:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] ppc: add AltiVec blend_bitmaps

altivec_utils.h collects the shared helpers: unaligned loads built from
vec_lvsl, lane windows and deinterleaves expressed as vec_perm rather
than vec_sld, the exact floor halving add base VMX lacks, and the
byte-lane masks used for row tails.

add_bitmaps/imul_bitmaps take an unaligned dst, but vec_st can only
write aligned quadwords, so the loops walk the aligned blocks covering
the row and shift the source into place instead; bytes outside the row
segment are masked to zero, which makes both operations the identity
there, exactly as the NEON backend does.  mul_bitmaps masks its result
instead and writes zeros past width.
---
 libass/ppc/altivec_utils.h         | 186 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libass/ppc/blend_bitmaps_altivec.c | 202 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 388 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libass/ppc/altivec_utils.h
 create mode 100644 libass/ppc/blend_bitmaps_altivec.c

